When attribution is required
----------------------------
Attribution is required only when you publicly claim conformance — for
example by stating that a product, report, or implementation "complies with",
"conforms to", "passes", "is certified under", or is "compatible with"
MGP-1.0 / Memory Gate Protocol 1.0.

Merely implementing the protocol, forking this repository, or shipping code
that follows the rules does NOT by itself require attribution.

Recommended attribution string:

  Conforms to Memory Gate Protocol (MGP) 1.0,
  specification by chenhz01 (Zhengming) —
  https://github.com/chenhz01/memory-gate-suite/blob/main/PROTOCOL.md

Machine-readable equivalent: "protocol": "mgp/1.0", "provider": "chenhz01".

